        "original_id": "d5c26efc-19ed-5a4c-a963-32ab9e1f9216",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Michigan gubernatorial election, 2006; Michigan Secretary of State election, 2014\n- People: Jennifer Granholm; Dick DeVos; Ruth Johnson\n- Roles: Governor of Michigan; lieutenant governor candidate; Michigan Secretary of State; Michigan House of Representatives member\n\nFacts:\n- The Michigan gubernatorial election of 2006 was one of 36 U.S. gubernatorial elections held on November 7, 2006.\n- Incumbent Democratic Governor Jennifer Granholm was re-elected in the 2006 Michigan gubernatorial election over Republican businessman Dick DeVos and three minor party candidates.\n- In 2006, Ruth Johnson was the Republican candidate for lieutenant governor as Dick DeVos's running mate.\n- Ruth Johnson was a former member of the Michigan House of Representatives.\n- Dick DeVos, born October 21, 1955, is an American entrepreneur, businessman, and author from Michigan.\n- In 2014, incumbent Republican Michigan Secretary of State Ruth Johnson was re-elected to a second term with 53.53% of the vote.",
